\pard \fs48
{\plain \fs48 \f2\fs48 A Thanksgiving for the Birth\par
}{\plain \fs48 \f2\fs48 or Adoption of a Child}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 As soon as convenient after the birth of a child, or after receiving a\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 child by adoption, the parents, with other members of the family, should\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 come to the church to be welcomed by the congregation and to give thanks\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 to Almighty God. It is desirable that this take place at a Sunday\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 service.  In the Eucharist it may follow the Prayers of the People\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 preceding the Offertory. At Morning or Evening Prayer it may take place\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 before the close of the Office.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 When desired, a briefer form of this service may be used, especially in\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 the hospital or at home; in which case the Celebrant may begin with the\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 Act of Thanksgiving, or with the prayer {\u8220\'93}O God, you have taught us.{\u8221\'94} A\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 passage from Scripture may first be read. Either Luke 2:41-51, or Luke\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 18:15-17, is appropriate.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 During the prayers, some parents may wish to express thanks in their}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 own words.\par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20  \par
}\pard \fs20
{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 At the proper time, the Celebrant invites the parents and other members\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 of the family to present themselves before the Altar.}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
