\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \b\f2 For the Birth of a Child}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 The Celebrant addresses the congregation in these or similar words}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f2 Dear Friends:  The birth of a child is a joyous and solemn\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 occasion in the life of a family. It is also an occasion for\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 rejoicing in the Christian community. I bid you, therefore,\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 to join }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N.}{\plain \fs24 \f2  [and }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 .] in giving thanks to Almighty God our\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 heavenly Father, the Lord of all life, for the gift of }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 . to be\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 their son (daughter) [and with }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 . (and }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 NN}{\plain \fs24 \f2 .), for a new\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 brother (sister)].  Let us say together:\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 The service continues with the Magnificat or one of the Psalms on pages\par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 441-443.}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f2 For an Adoption}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f2\fs20 The Celebrant addresses the congregation in these or similar words}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
}\pard \fs24\sl120\slmult1 
{\plain \fs24 \f2  \par
}\pard \fs24
{\plain \fs24 \f2 Dear Friends:  It has pleased God our heavenly Father to\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 answer the earnest prayers of }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 . [and }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 .], member(s) of this\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 Christian family, for the gift of a child. I bid you join with\par
}{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 them}{\plain \fs24 \f2  [and with }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 . (and }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 NN}{\plain \fs24 \f2 .), who now }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 has}{\plain \fs24 \f2  a new brother\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 (sister)] in offering heartfelt thanks for the joyful and solemn\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 responsibility which is }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 theirs}{\plain \fs24 \f2  by the coming of }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 N}{\plain \fs24 \f2 . to be a\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 member of }{\plain \fs24 \i\f2 their}{\plain \fs24 \f2  family.  But first, our friends wish us, here\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 assembled, to witness the inauguration of this new\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 relationship.\par
}{\plain \fs24 \f2 \par
